---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="skills" title="Skills">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Tool form 03B</p>
      <h1>Skills package repeatable know-how.</h1>
      <p>
        A skill is more than an instruction. It can bundle procedure, examples,
        scripts, templates, and domain constraints so the agent performs a
        workflow the same way every time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-grid">
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Use when</span>
        <h3>The work has a method.</h3>
        <p>
          Skills fit recurring workflows: render a document, analyze a dataset,
          prepare a release note, run a diagnostics playbook, or follow a
          company-specific review process.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Include</span>
        <h3>Instructions plus assets.</h3>
        <p>
          Put the core procedure in one readable guide. Add scripts for
          mechanical steps, templates for output shape, and examples that show
          what good execution looks like.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Design for</span>
        <h3>Triggering and scope.</h3>
        <p>
          Make it obvious when the skill should be used, what it owns, and when
          it should stop. The best skills reduce ambiguity without hiding the
          work.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <figure class="code-card">
      <figcaption>
        <span>google_adk_skill_toolset.py</span>
        <a href="https://adk.dev/skills/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Google ADK docs</a>
      </figcaption>
      <pre><code>import pathlib

from google.adk import Agent
from google.adk.skills import load_skill_from_dir
from google.adk.tools import skill_toolset

diagnostics_skill = load_skill_from_dir(
    pathlib.Path(__file__).parent / "skills" / "manufacturing-diagnostics"
)

diagnostics_tools = skill_toolset.SkillToolset(
    skills=[diagnostics_skill],
    additional_tools=[read_alarm_history, fetch_sensor_window],
)

root_agent = Agent(
    model="gemini-flash-latest",
    name="diagnostics_agent",
    instruction="Use the diagnostics skill before proposing maintenance.",
    tools=[diagnostics_tools],
)</code></pre>
    </figure>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
